;t7V@M{~WM{V@t8", "full_resolution": [1254, 1254]}, "title": "Parenting tip 214: How to respond if a child comes out to you.", "last_comment_created": 1786148481896, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 10, "score_up": 124, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATC9TIlK1", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 164, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "hat", "id": 8768755, "raw_content": "Finishing up our Costco run on Grant St. in Tucson Wednesday, and while getting ready to leave I noticed an elderly couple at a cafe table.  The man, looked like he had been rode hard and put away wet, probably been through some shit in his life including a few foreign wars...He had on an old plain white tee, and blue jeans, and an old and well worn MAKE AMERICA GREAT AGAIN baseball cap on his head.  I moved closer to him and got his attention, and said, \"We LOVE your hat! Wear it proudly!\" He seemed a little taken aback, and though I didn't notice, my wife said other people were sneering at us and him while we interacted.  Right before I started to turn and walk away it was obvious that he was choking up that I said that to him.  My wife said she thought he was about to cry.  I hope he has a wonderful remainder of his life, and I hope we can fix this shit for people like him who have suffered through life way more than my whiny ass has. ", "author": "BahamaDon", "created": 1786133312534, "profile_picture": "tTItVoXTx2D5", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "greenlandbettajoin", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_sou